            <section class="info-section" id="try">
                <h2>Trying it out</h2>
                <p>Open a profile with fictional details, or start a guest profile from the homepage. Guest profiles arrive with a few months of sample activity — accounts in two currencies, cards, payees, goals and, when market data is available, a small portfolio — so every screen has something to show.</p>
                <p>You can also load the same sample activity into a new profile during sign-up, or later from the dashboard.</p>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="market">
                <h2>Market data</h2>
                <p>A small Python service retrieves delayed quotes, price history, company profiles and headlines through the open-source yfinance library, and caches them briefly. If it can’t reach the data source, Willow shows “Market data temporarily unavailable.” rather than an estimate. Demo trades are blocked until fresh prices return.</p>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="assistant">
                <h2>The Willow Hub assistant</h2>
                <p>The assistant in Willow Hub answers a fixed set of questions about your money — spending, income, balances, net worth, goals, upcoming payments and investments — by calculating directly from your stored records. It does not use a language model, browse the web or make predictions, and it tells you when a question is outside what it can answer.</p>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="labels">
                <h2>Labels you’ll see</h2>
                <p>Look for the <span class="demo-badge">Demo</span> badge in the app, “Simulated” notes on receipts, and “Delayed” on prices. A full list is on the <a class="text-link" href="/compliance#labels">disclosures page</a>.</p>
            </section>
